A||||22||rodmcneill||Insurance rates?||||1||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||11-30-2000||11:09 AM||||I was wondering what other members of the Forum are paying for their insurance rates? I am presently with State Farm 47 years old good driving record(!) have 2 GTs insured with them (multi car disc.) and average about $270.00 per 6 month (full coverage). If we get other examples of what other members are paying maybe this will help direct someone to a company with lower rates. Remember to give your age and driving record(if its not too bad!) PS I do not sell insurance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||11-30-2000||11:14 AM||||I am 37, good record, married, 86 SE insured as a collectable for appraised value, $109 per 6 months. (Before apprasied value and collectable status it was $116/6 months)<BR>Collectable status allows me 3400 miles per year and exempt from emission testing.<BR>Nationwide Insurance.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-30-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||the need for speed||11-30-2000||11:27 AM||||I am with allstate and have two cars on my policy,the 87 pontiac fiero gt and a 89 toyota SR5 extra cab 4x4 truck.i am 25 and have two speeding tickets in the last 3 years no more than ten miles over on both.I have the basic rates and am paying $119 a month. was going to start looking around to see if i could find some thing lower,who is a good company to go with?||||reg||1
Z||000003||rodmcneill||11-30-2000||12:28 PM||||By the way the $270.00 I am paying per 6 months is for each vehicle not both. Another reason I wanted this info was that GM. as one of the reasons they dropped the Fiero was insurance rates were getting very high for the Fiero. This goes back to the late 80s. I was just wondering what younger drivers are paying nowadays.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||11-30-2000||01:14 PM||||I'm 43, married, with a good driving record. (Last ticket was probably three years ago. Not sure if State Farm ever checked.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>My insurance is about $330/6 months for the Formula, and $310 for the coupe. My 92 Sonoma is very similar in price. Full coverage. Multi-car and multi-line discount.<P>Raydar||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||11-30-2000||01:50 PM||||I was paying $500 a year for 3 cars- From when I was 16-18 (now I have no coverage on either fiero right now since it's winter) But I wasn't the "full time driver"- so I'm sure that lowered my rates. That worked out to about $42 a month for a Fiero coupe, a Subaru, and a conversion van. I've never had any moving violations so right now it's extremely cheap for me. It was with Reliant Insurance, and that's only in Ohio.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnnyK||11-30-2000||04:10 PM||||I WAS paying about $1900 a year. But now, after my stop sign running car totalling shenaningans, I'm sure it's up there. Before that, I wanted to get an MR2, I inquired, and it would have been $9500 a year. Yikes.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||11-30-2000||04:58 PM||||Wow!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Just wait until you try to buy insurance for the Delorean. They're going to eat you alive. I hope I'm wrong, though.||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||11-30-2000||05:09 PM||||i'm only on liability and it's 55 a month. it kinda sucks being my age when paying for insurance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  but i did get one ticket one time for racing, and my insurance didn't go up any.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>i don't think i've raced since that day.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rodrv6||11-30-2000||05:20 PM||||I'm 42, single, and haven't had a ticket in the last 5 years.  I use State Farm for all three of my vehicles, 84 Fiero (liability), 92 Maxima (liability), and 66 Porsche 911 (full coverage comprehensive, under 12,000 miles/year).  My cost for all three is around $95/month.  I am very pleased with State Farm.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting :)||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroMaster88||11-30-2000||06:07 PM||||I have an 88 coupe, i am 19 (almost20) and for full coverage it costs me about $500 every 6 months.  I had 1 ticked but they never cought on!!!  The company i go through is State Farm.||||reg||1
Z||000011||stsmithgt||12-01-2000||09:39 AM||||I have Farmers Ins.  It's about 210 every 6 months for liability only.  I had a ticket I went to traffic school for about three years ago.  Some cop was passing out tickets for B.S. reasons that day. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> I think he was hoping for a chase, but I disappointed him.  Other than that, I haven't had a ticket for 10 years before that.  My friends find that hard to believe.  I think I'm paying too much for so little being 39 yrs old, but I'm not getting around to doing much about it at this time.||||reg||1
Z||000012||AkursedX||12-01-2000||10:11 AM||||I'm 20, and I have just liability on the GT, and it cost me about 125/month, or 750/6 months.  And that is with a 15% good student discount.  I've had no tickets and no accidents.  And that is the cheapest I could find!  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||ThatRickGuy||12-01-2000||12:12 PM||||my 88 formula runs my $65/month(pay 10 months, 2 months free), ticket free 21 yr old male w/ integon, in the Northern VA/ Washington DC area (I-95). <P>And on a side note, the reson why Fieros were so expensive to insure in the 80's wasn't because of the 'sportyness' of them. it was because of theft rates. The people who only had liability didn't get hit by hard insurance, but most 18-28yr olds buy vehicles w/ car loans which means full coverage, so they were getting hit hard for the theft insurance.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Daniel87GT||12-01-2000||12:26 PM||||I pay about $90/6-months/1 car/Liabilty only through Progressive. You can get a quote yourself at <A HREF="http://www.progressive.com" TARGET=_blank>www.progressive.com</A>  You may be able to get a better quote by talking to them directly on the phone, esp. if you want full coverage on an "old" Fiero.<P>BTW. I used to sell insurance for a living<P>My experience with insurance: Shop arround. Most people that I've met that have insurance with Farmers or State Farm were at one time getting a good rate, but are now paying to much for their situation.  AllState is usually a good insurer (rates & service). Progressive is quite good.  <P>My recommendation:  any time something happens that changes your insurance situation, go shopping for rates.  e.g. you get married, buy a house, get a second car, get older, tickets on or off of your record, or if it has been a year since you last checked.<P>Remember though.  Not all insurance companies are the same.  Some are rated A+, some are not.  There are insurers that have great rates that I wouldn't touch with a ten foot pole.||||reg||6
Z||000015||PAUL88GT||12-01-2000||06:51 PM||||I am paying about $110 every 6 months with State Farm.  However, it is classified as a classic car and I am limited to about 2000 miles per year.<P>I am 40'ish with a very clean driving record.<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 12-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||CUTTER||12-02-2000||02:32 AM||||My 91 MR2 turbo is $2065 a year full coverage with erie insurance||||reg||1
